1. Reads records (byte strings split by `\n`) from stdin
2. Sorts them in unsigned bytewise lexicographic order
3. Outputs each record followed by `\n`
4. Rejects any arguments (except bare `--`) with exit 2 and a stderr diagnostic
5. Handles all edge cases (empty input, empty records, NUL bytes, invalid UTF-8)

